==English==
{{was wotd|2017|April|2}}

===Etymology===
From the idea that a dead cat dropped from a height might bounce without this indicating any actual sign of life.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|/dɛd kæt baʊns/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|trading}} A [[temporary]] [[recovery]] in the [[price]] of an [[instrument]] the [[price]] of which has [[fall#Verb|fallen]] [[rapidly]] and is [[expect#Verb|expected]] to fall [[further]] [[in the long run]].

